# 🩺 CKD Prediction Web App | Machine Learning + Flask

## 1. 📌 Project Overview

The **CKD Prediction Web App** is a Machine Learning-based healthcare application developed to predict the possibility of **Chronic Kidney Disease (CKD)** using selected clinical parameters.

The project combines **Machine Learning, Python, Flask, SQL/SQLite, HTML, CSS, and JavaScript** to create an interactive web-based prediction system.

The application allows users to:

- Create an account and sign in.
- Enter patient clinical information.
- Submit clinical parameters to the trained Machine Learning model.
- Generate a CKD prediction.
- Store patient information and prediction results.
- View patient-related records.
- Generate a PDF report containing patient and prediction information.

The main purpose of this project is to demonstrate how a Machine Learning model can be integrated into a complete web application rather than being used only as a standalone Python program.

### Project Highlights

- Machine Learning-based CKD prediction
- Flask web application
- Clinical data preprocessing
- Trained model saved using Joblib
- SQLite database integration
- Patient record management
- User authentication
- PDF report generation
- Flask-Migrate database migrations
- Interactive web interface
- End-to-end ML application workflow

---

## 2. 🧩 Problem Statement

Chronic Kidney Disease is a condition in which the kidneys gradually lose their ability to function properly. Early identification of potential CKD can be useful because kidney-related conditions may develop gradually and may not always show obvious symptoms in their early stages.

Traditional diagnosis involves clinical evaluation, laboratory tests, medical history, and professional interpretation.

This project explores the use of **Machine Learning techniques to analyze selected clinical parameters and generate a CKD prediction**.

The system provides a web-based interface where clinical values can be entered and processed by a trained Machine Learning model.

The project demonstrates how data preprocessing, Machine Learning, database management, and web development can be combined to create an end-to-end predictive application.

> **Note:** This application is an educational and demonstration project. It is not a medical diagnostic system and should not be used as a replacement for professional medical advice.

---

## 3. 🎯 Objectives

The major objectives of the project are:

### Machine Learning Objectives

- Develop a Machine Learning model for CKD prediction.
- Prepare and preprocess clinical data.
- Select relevant clinical parameters for prediction.
- Train the model using the prepared dataset.
- Save the trained model for application integration.
- Use the trained model to generate predictions from new patient data.

### Web Application Objectives

- Develop a user-friendly web interface using Flask.
- Provide registration and login functionality.
- Create a patient information form.
- Connect the web application with the Machine Learning model.
- Display prediction results to the user.
- Store patient information and prediction results.
- Generate patient PDF reports.

### Database Objectives

- Store patient-related information.
- Manage application data using SQLite.
- Define database models using Flask-SQLAlchemy.
- Manage database schema changes using Flask-Migrate and Alembic.

### Learning Objectives

This project provides practical experience in:

- Python programming
- Data preprocessing
- Machine Learning
- Flask development
- SQL/database concepts
- HTML/CSS/JavaScript
- Model integration
- CRUD-style database operations
- Application deployment concepts

---

## 4. 🛠️ Technologies Used

| Technology | Purpose |
|---|---|
| Python | Application development and Machine Learning |
| Pandas | Data loading and preprocessing |
| Scikit-learn | Machine Learning model development |
| Joblib | Saving and loading the trained model |
| Flask | Backend web application framework |
| Flask-SQLAlchemy | Database integration |
| Flask-Migrate | Database migration management |
| Alembic | Database schema migration |
| Flask-Mail | Email-related functionality |
| SQLite | Application database |
| HTML | Web page structure |
| CSS | Web page styling |
| JavaScript | Client-side interaction |
| PDFKit | PDF generation |
| Git/GitHub | Version control and project hosting |

